WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.760
Night in Venice.

2
00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:05.360
Armed men surround a
general, swords drawn.

3
00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:07.500
He doesn't even raise his voice.

4
00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:11.280
"Keep up your bright swords,
for the dew will rust them."

5
00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:12.520
Act 5.

6
00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:15.450
The same soldier stands
by a curtained bed.

7
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:18.130
He calls himself "An honourable murderer,

8
00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:19.310
if you will."

9
00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:20.960
A calm commander.

10
00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:22.800
A man who has killed.

11
00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:25.170
Which one is the real Othello?

12
00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:28.860
In this mission, you'll study
the authority he shows in Act 1,

13
00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:30.670
in front of the whole senate.

14
00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:34.910
You'll track how his language changes,
right up to the speech where he tells Venice

15
00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:36.530
how to remember him.

16
00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:40.450
And you'll weigh two critics
who read him in opposite ways.

17
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:44.140
Your mission: decide
which is the real Othello.
